hw/rtl/ - synthesisable RTL
===========================

VHDL-2008, one entity per file, elaborated in this order (see hw.mk SRCS):

    cgra_pkg.vhd      constants + types + functions. THE protocol/config-word
                      contract: opcodes, operand selects, command bytes, checksum
                      rules. Mirror of lib/include/cgra.h and lib/src/emu.c.
                      Records: pe_neigh_t (the N/S/E/W operand bundle) and
                      cfg_fields_t (a decoded config word); decode_cfg() splits a
                      raw word into fields, cfg_word() packs one.
    cgra_comp_pkg.vhd component declarations for every block below, so the
                      structural parents instantiate by component (not by
                      entity). Mirror each entity's ports exactly.
    uart_rx.vhd       8N1 receiver, two-flop input sync, mid-bit sampling.
                      rx_valid pulses one clock per received byte.
    uart_tx.vhd       8N1 transmitter. Pulse tx_start while tx_busy = '0'.
    pe.vhd            the processing element: neigh (pe_neigh_t) + decode_cfg ->
                      two operand muxes -> 16-bit ALU -> one step-gated register.
    cgra_array.vhd    G_ROWS x G_COLS mesh of pe (generics default to the package
                      geometry; positive dimensions set the port bounds).
                      Interior PEs read their
                      N/S/E/W neighbours; north/west edges take the input ports,
                      south/east edges read zero. Instantiates pe by component.
    cgra_ctrl.vhd     protocol FSM: ID / CFG / WR / RUN / RD / RST / EXEC,
                      checksum verify, watchdog. EXEC (protocol v3) is the fused
                      transaction -- edge inputs, an optional datapath clear, N
                      steps and a MASKED register read-back in one round trip;
                      it shares the S_WR payload path and the S_RUN step engine
                      with the unfused commands rather than duplicating them
                      (wr_ret / run_ret say where each returns). The PE
                      read-back mux is registered into rd_word before the
                      checksum adder, so word_idx -> cksum is a mux OR an adder
                      per clock, never both. Issues 'step' once every G_STEP_DIV
                      clocks (generic, default 2), making the ALU datapath a
                      G_STEP_DIV-cycle multicycle path (see scr/constraints.tcl).
                      One step is always one result, so raising G_STEP_DIV lets
                      the clock run faster without touching emu.c. The make knob
                      STEP_DIV drives both this generic and the XDC number.
    cgra_top.vhd      G_ROWS/G_COLS propagate to controller and array (default
                      4x4; complete device supports at most 16 16-bit PEs).
                      The ID response reports these dimensions.
                      Top level: clk + reset sync + UART + ctrl + array + LEDs.
                      Instantiates the four blocks by component.

Conventions
-----------
- Active-high synchronous reset, everything on rising_edge(clk).
- Signals lower_snake, constants UPPER, generics G_*, states S_*.
- Types/records in cgra_pkg; components in cgra_comp_pkg; the PE output register
  is named 'r' (synthesises to r_reg -- the multicycle XDC selector matches it).
- No vendor primitives: portable across Xilinx parts and GHDL.

Editing cgra_pkg.vhd? It is a three-way contract - update the C header and
the emulator to match, or `make test` on the host will diverge from silicon.

The controller retains a 16-bit EXEC mask for every geometry. Mask bits beyond
the PE count are ignored on the wire and rejected by the host API. Its shared
word index covers max(R*C, R+C), with a guarded PE read mux for single-row and
single-column arrays. MESH_ROWS/MESH_COLS drive both Vivado generic arguments
and the output directory; see doc/mesh-generalization.md.
